      "description": "Overlap area in steradians (unit sphere) of two convex spherical polygons with great-circle edges: cell `cell_a` of the `[cells, nv_a, 3]` unit-vector stack `ring_a` and cell `cell_b` of `ring_b` (build a stack from lon-lat degrees with `lonlat_to_unit`). The value of `polygon_intersection_area` with `manifold: \"spherical\"` (or `\"geodesic\"`, the same great-circle model) within the CONFORMANCE_SPEC §5.8.2 tolerance; multiply by R^2 for a physical area. Either ring orientation (the interior is the side of less than a hemisphere); repeated vertices contribute exactly zero. Half-space tests are linear in the chord parameter; each clipped edge contributes the signed area of the spherical triangle it spans with the first vertex of `ring_a` (Van Oosterom-Strackee, `atan2`). A half-space test within 1e-14 of zero counts as on the great circle. Each polygon must lie within a hemisphere; non-convex input is outside the contract.",
